  "term": "aldosterone",
  "definition": "Aldosterone is a biological substance found in the blood that, in this source, is linked to motion sickness. Higher aldosterone levels and aldosterone administration were associated with motion sickness-like responses and increased inner-ear endolymph volume, effects that were reduced by atrial natriuretic peptide.",
